ggml from llama.cpp b12177 (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp, MIT, LICENSE beside this file; b11724 before 2026-11-06), with the
pause points that src/metal/patch_ggml_pause.py adds (build.sh applies it; it does nothing to a copy already patched)
and Momoe's CUDA additions: the mailbox ops (include/ggml-momoe-mailbox.h, src/ggml-cuda/momoe-mailbox.cu*),
ggml_backend_cuda_buffer_from_host, GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_GRAPHS read at each call, MOMOE_CUDA_DUMP, a CUDA graph whose
executable does not fit in the free VRAM freeing the others' (momoe_graph_instantiate; b12177's chunked graphs leave no
place for the old fallback of running the captured kernels directly), the MUL_MAT_ID ids helper's generic path giving
every use of an expert its own column when a token uses one more than once (MOMOE_MMID_REPEATS); and Metal's
kernel_mul_mm_id_map0 for 9 experts a token (Nemotron 3.5 Bolt's: b11724 has none, so its prompts failed on Macs).
